#. module: l10n_mx_edi_blacklist
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_l10n_mx_edi_blacklist
msgid ""
"===========================\n"
"Mexican EDI - SAT Blacklist\n"
"===========================\n"
"\n"
".. \n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! This file is generated by oca-gen-addon-readme !!\n"
"   !! changes will be overwritten.                   !!\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"   !! source digest: sha256:582ad87491a29c3f5b402ca1358d8ff9e08ec0f96c6e6be22e7a65317ef8284a\n"
"   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Beta-yellow.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Beta\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/license-LGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: LGPL-3\n"
".. |badge3| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/github-amxodoo%2Fenterprise-lightgray.png?logo=github\n"
"    :target: https://github.com/amxodoo/enterprise/tree/20.0/l10n_mx_edi_blacklist\n"
"    :alt: amxodoo/enterprise\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3|\n"
"\n"
"Block CFDI stamping of customer invoices and credit notes when the\n"
"customer RFC is on the SAT blacklist of article 69-B of the CFF\n"
"(Presunto or Definitivo).\n"
"\n"
"The check runs before the invoice is sent to the PAC. When the RFC is\n"
"listed, Odoo stops stamping with an error dialog and posts the same text\n"
"on the invoice chatter, including the official SAT reference (número y\n"
"fecha de oficio). Taxpayers published as Desvirtuado or Sentencia\n"
"Favorable are not blocked.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"This module depends on Mexican EDI (``l10n_mx_edi``), which is part of\n"
"Odoo Enterprise, and on ``l10n_mx_sat_69b`` for the SAT article 69-B\n"
"list.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"No configuration is required.\n"
"\n"
"The SAT list is downloaded by ``l10n_mx_sat_69b``. Generic RFCs\n"
"``XAXX010101000`` and ``XEXX010101000``, and invoices sent to the\n"
"general public, are not checked.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"1. Install **Mexican EDI - SAT Blacklist** on a company that already\n"
"   uses Mexican EDI.\n"
"2. Confirm a customer invoice (or credit note) whose partner RFC is a\n"
"   real taxpayer RFC.\n"
"3. Send the CFDI the usual way (Send & Print, or the CFDI retry action).\n"
"4. When the RFC is **Presunto** or **Definitivo** on SAT list 69-B:\n"
"\n"
"   - the CFDI is not stamped;\n"
"   - a dialog shows the customer, the RFC, the SAT status, and the\n"
"     official reference (oficio);\n"
"   - the same text stays on the invoice chatter.\n"
"\n"
"5. When the RFC is not on the list, or is **Desvirtuado** or **Sentencia\n"
"   Favorable**, stamping continues as usual.\n"
"6. When the SAT list cannot be downloaded and there is no cached copy,\n"
"   the invoice is not stamped and the chatter explains that the\n"
"   blacklist could not be verified.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/amxodoo/enterprise/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
